! ^

Use ! to repeat the last command typed at the keyboard.

Use ^ to replace a string from the last command with a new string.  The
syntax is the same as in unix: "^old-string^replacement"

Examples:

  > tell rasmusse Hi there, how are you?
  No-one by that name here.

  > ^rasmusse^rasmussen
  You tell Rasmussen, 'Hi there, how are you?'

  > ^you^you doing^
  You tell Rasmussen, 'Hi there, how are you doing?'

See Also: ALIAS
#
ABILITIES ABILITY

Usage: abilities <ability>

By itself, this command will display your current ability scores in the
following format:

   Your current ability scores: 
    Strength:      ( 18) (828)
    Dexterity:     ( 12) (135)
    Intelligence:  ( 13) (170)
    Wisdom:        (  9) (90)
    Constitution:  ( 18) (828)
    Charisma:      ( 16) (450)

Ability values can vary depending on how you have customized your character,
and the cost in experience to increase an ability by one point is displayed
on the far right.

By specifying an ability in the command line, you can increase that ability
by one point provided you have enough unassigned experience and available
"points". You gain one point per level.

Example:
  > abilities str
    Increases your strength by one point, and subtracts 828 points from your
    unassigned experience.

See Also: EXPERIENCE
#
AID FIRST "FIRST AID"

Usage: aid <victim>

Use this skill to help incapacitated friends. This only works on characters
who are almost dead, however.
#
AMBUSH

Usage: ambush <victim>

With superior knowledge of the lay of the land, a player can prepare a
sneaky ambush for his enemies. You can only ambush someone where there is 
enough cover to hide, of course.  If you can successfully ambush someone
while staying hidden, you increase the damage dealt to them.

See Also: HIDE
#
ALIAS ALIASES

Usage: alias [alias name] [command]

An alias is a single command used to represent one or more other commands.
The ALIAS command can be used to manipulate your character's aliases.  Type
ALIAS alone to see a list of your currently defined aliases.

  > alias

Type ALIAS <alias name> <command> to create a new alias.  The alias name must
be one word.  The command can be any string.  Aliases may not be nested or
used recursively.  Any command may be overridden by an alias (other than the
ALIAS command itself, of course).

  > alias gbb get bread bag
  > alias gac get all corpse

Type ALIAS <alias-name> to delete an alias that has already been defined.

  > alias gbb

A semicolon (";") can be used to define multiple actions to be taken with
a single alias.

  > alias eat get bread bag; eat bread

Note that the 'eat' contained within the eat alias is interpreted as the MUD's
internal eat command; aliases may not be nested or used recursively.  The
variables $1, $2, ... $9 may be used to represent arguments given with
an alias.

Examples:

  > alias killem cast 'fireball' $1; cast 'harm' $2
  > killem fido mage

Would cast fireball on fido, followed by casting harm on mage.  Variables
may be used repeatedly and in any order:

  > alias helpem cast 'heal' $1; cast 'bless' $1; cast 'armor' $1

The special variable $* represents the entire input line after an alias:

  > alias tr tell rasmussen $*
  > tr hi there, how are you today?
  You tell Rasmussen, 'hi there, how are you today?'

See Also: ! ^
#
ANSI COLOR

Usage: color [off | sparse | normal | complete]

If you have a color-capable terminal and wish to see useful color-coding
of information, use the COLOR command to set the level of coloring you see.

  > color off
  This command disables all color.

  > color sparse
  > color normal
  > color complete

These three commands turn color on to various levels.  Experiment to see
which level suits your personal taste.

'color' with no argument will display your current color level.
'color on' defaults to 'complete'.

Using color will slow down the speed at which you see messages VERY slightly.
The effect is more noticeable on slower connections.  Even if you have
color turned on, non-colorized messages will not be slowed down at all.

See Also: COLORSPRAY "COLOR SPRAY"
#
APPRAISE

Usage	: appraise <object in inventory>
Example	: appraise sword
		  appraise 2.dagger

A successful appraisal gives an item value within 20 or so coins.
Unsuccessful appraisals can be much, much worse.

#
ASSIST

Usage: ASSIST <person in need>

If Quifael is being beaten senseless by a warg and you feel brave enough
to help him, type ASSIST QUIFAEL to hit the warg.  Note that the warg will
keep hitting Quifael; assist only makes you start to fight whomever the
person you're assisting is fighting.

  > assist Quifael

See Also: FLEE KILL RESCUE
#
AUCTION CHANNEL CHANNELS GOSSIP GRATS NOAUCTION NOGOSSIP NOGRATS

Usage: auction <message>
       gossip <message>
       grats <message>
       newbie <message>

These are channels reserved for specific purposes.  Messages on these
channels reach everyone who is monitoring them.  You must be at least level
two to use these channels, except the newbie channel.

To turn a channel on and off, use the TOGGLE command.

Examples:
  > auction short sword -- minimum bid 100k
  > gossip Hey, is that a short sword on your belt or are you happy to see me?
  > grats LEVEL!!!!!!!!
  > grats GRATS CATJE!!!!!!!!
  > newbie Damn, where's the donation room?
  > newbie Help me please, any high levelers listening?

See Also: EMOTE GSAY HOLLER SAY SHOUT TOGGLE
#
AUTO

Usage: auto [ <option> ]

When used alone, "auto" will show what handy automatic features you are
using.  When used with an option (see down a few lines) it will toggle that
option for you.

The options available are:
	exits		Show exits in room descriptions
	loot		Strip the equipment, including gold, off a fresh kill
	gold		Strip the gold off a fresh kill
	split		Split the loot with your group

Note: To use AUTO SPLIT, AUTO GOLD must be set.

See Also: TOGGLE
#
BACKSTAB

Usage	: backstab <victim>

Backstab is a way to sneak up on a person and attempt to place your dagger
in his back, at exactly the point where it does most damage.  A successful
backstab gives a damage multiplier, depending on level.

The chance of successfully backstabbing a person depends on how high your
skill level is. Also, backstabbing a person will lag you for about two
rounds of combat.
#
BANK WITHDRAW DEPOSIT BALANCE

Commands to take money out of the bank, put money in the bank, or see how
much money you have in the bank.

Examples:

  > deposit 400
  > withdraw 1000
  > balance

See Also: GOLD SCORE
#
BASH

The success of a bash depends upon how well you are learned.  To bash someone
is to attempt to 'knock' that person over.  If you succeed you will inflict
minor damage, and cause the victim to fall on it's rear.  The victim will be
unable to issue any commands for 2 rounds of violence.  If you miss you lose
your balance and fall.

A bash makes you unable to type commands for 2 rounds of violence.

See Also: KICK RESCUE
#
BIND

While adventuring in the world of Dark Pawns you may find it convient at times
to BIND your spirit to specific locations within the game.  Once bound, your
physical body will be resurrected at the bind point should you die.  Magics
that 'recall' you will also recall you to the last place you bound.

You may bind in any place that is filled with a "warm blue glow", such as
the Temple of the Cross in Kir Drax'in.
#
BEARHUG

Usage: bearhug <victim>

By using this skill, the combatant can grab their adversary in a rib-breaking squeeze,
slowing them down during combat.  Note that this also slows you down as well.
#
BEHEAD

Usage:  behead corpse

Lets you take home a trophy from your kill....
Beheads the corpse of your fallen adversary and places it in your inventory.
#
BERSERK

Usage: berserk

Lose your control and let your battle rage take over... While berserking you 
care less about your own safety, but inflict a barrage of damaging blows to 
thy enemies.
Berserking can only be attempted successfully once every two game hours
(ticks).
#
BITE

Usage	: bite <victim>

In the case of vampires, this is a mere side-affect, as using the bite command
to suck the blood of their victim is a common and natural thing, as the blood
suffuses them with life and satiates their almost voracious appetites.

See Also: VAMPIRE WEREWOLF TRANSFORM
#
BRIEF

Usage: brief

Toggle "brief mode".  When in brief mode, you don't see the descriptions of
the room you are in; only the name of the room and the people and objects
there.  Unless you're very familiar with the area in which you're traveling,
however, it is not advisable to use this command.  Frequently, you will find
small but vital hints in the descriptions of the rooms: An extra peek at your
surroundings could mean the difference between life and death!

If you explicitly type 'look', you will always see the full room description,
even in BRIEF mode.

Looking into other rooms by typing LOOK [direction] will appear in 
"brief mode" if brief is on.

See Also: COMPACT LOOK
#
BUG TYPO IDEA

Usage: bug <bug report>
       idea <your new idea>
       typo <that nasty typo>       

For making useful suggestions and reporting problems to the Powers that Be.

Examples:

  > bug the entire game crashes when I type 'put bag in bag'
  > idea make a restaurant in Kir-Oshi
  > typo 'sence' should be spelled 'sense'

There's no need to tell where the bug/typo is; We can tell what room you're
in.

 > typo there is no exit to the west here, but the descript says there is

#
BURY DIG

Usage: bury <object>
       dig

Used to bury your items and then retrieve them at a later date. The object can
be in your inventory or in the room, but if you can't take it, you won't be
able to bury it. Be warned, there are no tell-tale signs that you have buried
anything so you will need to remember where it was that you left the item.

You will need to locate a shovel if you plan to bury or dig...the best place to
look would be at your local general store.

Examples:

  > bury sword
  > dig
#
BUY

Usage: buy <item name>
       buy #<item number>
       buy n.<item name>
       buy n <item name>
       buy n #<item number>

If you'd like to purchase an item from a shop and have the money, you can buy
it.  Items can be bought by name, or by their number in the shop listing,
and can be bought in quantity.
 
Examples:
 
  > buy sword        (buy the first sword on the list)
  > buy #3           (buy the third item on the list)
  > buy 4.sword      (buy the fourth sword on the list)
  > buy 10 bread     (buy 10 pieces of bread)
  > buy 10 #2        (buy 10 of the second item on the list)
 
See Also: LIST SELL SHOPS VALUE
#
CARVE

Usage: carve corpse

Lets you carve up some dinner off of certain dead mobiles.
Typically, any type of animal should be able to be carved up for a nice tasty
dinner.

See Also: EAT FOOD
#
CHARGE

Usage: charge <victim>

The charge is offensive move, used to try to impale the victim. A successful
charge deals a great deal of damage, the only drawback being the recover-time
from a charge is quite lengthy.
#
CIRCLE

Usage	: 	circle <victim>

Use this command to circle behind an opponent and stab him in the back. This
is basically a form of backstab that can be used in battle but does less 
damage.  You can only attempt to circle when you are not being hit.

See Also: BACKSTAB
#
CLS

Clears the screen.
Note that in most clients, this typically erases scrollback.
#
COMMANDS

Usage: commands

The COMMANDS command gives a canonical list of all the known verbs.

Each command listed should have help available by typing "HELP <command>".

See Also: SOCIAL SOCIALS
#
COMPACT

Usage: compact

This command toggles the extra blank line output to your screen after each
command.  Useful if you have a small display.

See Also: BRIEF
#
COMPARE

Usage	: compare <item1> <item2>

Compare two weapons, or two pieces of armor of the same type.
#
CONSIDER

Usage: consider <monster>

This command gives a rough estimate of your opponent. Four things are 
considered: Your enemy's strength, health, level and your ability to
hit him/her. So while they may be very powerful, and be a much higher
level, they may be almost dead, etc.

Example:

  > consider fido

See Also: KILL
#
CUTTHROAT

Usage    : cutthroat <victim>
Duration : Varies with level

With the proper weapon, you can slit their throat, making it hard for them to 
fight, heal, and generally making life hell until they are healed by magickal 
means.
#
DIAGNOSE

Usage: diagnose [character]

The DIAGNOSE command tells you how wounded a character looks.  If you are
fighting someone, you can use DIAGNOSE with no arguments to diagnose the
person you're fighting. This can be particularly useful if looking at your
adversary has particularly nasty side effects.

Examples: 

  > diagnose
  > diagnose rasmussen

See Also: CONSIDER
#
DISARM

Usage: disarm

Calling upon your skills, you attempt to disarm your opponent. Failed
attempts are usually pretty messy.
#
DISEMBOWEL

Usage: disembowel <victim>

An experienced vagabond can slice open the stomach of a victim with the 
proper weapon, spilling their victim's guts everywhere. Performing this
procedure is tricky, however, and usually takes some time.
#
DISMOUNT

Usage: dismount

Used to get off of your favorite mode of transport.

See Also: MOUNT STABLE
#
PROMPT

Usage: prompt <string> or "default", "all", "none"

Dark Pawns features user-configurable prompts.  The prompt can display
whatever you would like, using the following variables:

$h - Your current hit points
$H - Your maximum hit points
$m - Your current mana
$M - Your maximum mana
$v - Your current stamina
$V - Your maximum stamina
$T - The status of the TANK
$F - The status of whatever you are currently fighting

Some examples:

"Classic DP Prompt"
Typing: prompt $hH $mM $vV>
Yields: 100H 100M 100V> as your prompt

"Default prompt"
Typing: prompt $h/$HH $m/$MM $v/$VV>
Yields: 100/100H 100/100M 100/100V> as your prompt

Additionally there are several quick prompt modes:

default - the default prompt, shown above
all     - all variables: $h/$HH $m/$MM $v/$VV $T $F>
none    - no variables, just >

#
DONATE

Usage: donate <object>
       donate <number> coins


This command takes an object that you no longer want and deposits it in the
donation room of all of the major cities to assist newbies in getting
started. There is an equal chance of the object being junked, or ending up
in the donation rooms of Kir Drax'in, Kir Oshi, Kir Morthis, Mist Keep or
Xixieqi.

  > donate shield
  > donate all.bread
  > donate 500 coins

See Also: JUNK
#
"DRAGON KICK" DRAGON

Usage: dragon <victim>

The secret attack of the Hidden Dragon school of ninjitsu, this powerful
upper body kick slams into the victim with devastating force, knocking 
backwards and leaving them dazed.

#
DRAW

Usage: draw <item>

Occassionally, the creatures of the land will carry one or more items that
you can claim following a battle. If you are part of a group, and one or
more of the party also want that item, you can DRAW for it in a lotto-
style system.

The individual using the DRAW command will summon a trader who will oversee
proceedings and keep the item until the DRAW is complete. Once all of the
members are present who wish to partake, the individual who entered the
command should follow the instructions of the trader to begin. (This is
usually simply saying "begin")

The trader will then randomly choose a member from the room and the item
shall be given to them.  To cancel a draw, the person who initiated it
should simply leave the room.

Example:
  
  Aneassa the trader states, 'When you are ready, let us begin.'
  
  > say begin

  Aneassa the trader states, 'Frontline has been chosen as the winner.'
  Frontline has received an ornate dagger from the draw.
#
DROP

Usage: drop <item>
       drop all.<item>
       drop all
       drop <number> coins

If you lose interest in a carried item, you can drop it on the ground.
You should always respect other players however and not leave your stuff 
littering the ground - you will find items that are left for an extended
period of time will magically be removed from the land. To get rid of items,
use JUNK or DONATE.

Note: Using this command in combat will add a delay to your next attack. The
heavier the object, the longer the delay before you can next cast a spell, use
a skill or hit with your weapon.

  > drop bottle
  > drop all.bread
  > drop all
  > drop 1000 coins

See Also: DONATE GET JUNK
#
EAT DRINK

Usage: eat <item>
       drink [from] <item>

If you're hungry or thirsty, these commands are for you!

  > eat bread
  > drink from cup

See Also: HUNGER THIRST
#
EMOTE

Usage: emote <message>
       : <message>

Show people what you're feeling.  The shorthand is ":".

"emote <string>" will display your name, then the string.

Example:

If your name is "Helt",

  > emote is feeling very sad today.

will display:

Helt is feeling very sad today.

See Also: SOCIALS
#
ENTER

Usage: enter <place>

If you type 'enter' while you are outdoors, you'll enter any nearby shelter.
You can also follow 'enter' with an argument; for example, 'enter window', or
'enter moongate'.
#
EXAMINE

Usage: examine <object | mobile>

May give you some valuable information about an item or monster.
A little more detailed than LOOK.

See Also: LOOK
#
EQUIPMENT

Usage: equipment

Gives you a list of all the equipment you're wearing, holding, and wielding.

See Also: INVENTORY REMOVE WEAR
#
EVASION

This skill will allow you to evade anyone who is tracking you, there is no
command to type; just learn the skill.
#
EXITS

Usage: exits

Gives you a list of the obvious exits from your location.  Of course, the less
obvious ones won't show up here - you have to THINK in order to locate those.

See Also: AUTO SEARCH
#
FILL

Usage: fill <item> <object to fill from>

If you want to fill a container you're holding with liquid from a fountain
in the same room as you.

Example:

  > fill canteen fountain

See Also: POUR DRINK
#
FINGER WHOIS

Usage	: finger <player name>
	  whois  <player name>

Lists the level, name and title of <player name>, if they exist.
#
FLEE

Usage: flee

If you are in a fight and things are beginning to get a little uncomfortable
(maybe you are dying), just type 'flee', and presto!  You are out of harms way
- that is, IF there is a suitable exit nearby, and IF that exit doesn't simply
bring you from the ashes to the fire... but then, who wants to live forever?

Note: As this is a combat command, it is affected by your combat wait (refer
to COMBAT for an explanation).

See Also: COMBAT WIMPY
#
FLESH ALTER "FLESH ALTER"

Usage: alter

Flesh alter allows the mentalist to manipulate the molecules in their arm,
hardening them into a weapon. While this skill is being used, no other weapon
may be wielded.
#
FOLLOW

Usage: follow <leader>

Use FOLLOW to automatically follow someone else.

Examples:

  > follow ras
  > follow self

See Also: GROUP SNEAK SHADOW
#
GET

Usage: get <object>
       get all
       get all.<object>
       get all.<object> in <object>

If you find something interesting on the ground, you may use 'get' to pick
it up. 'get' can also be used to extract items from containers.

Note: Using this command in combat will add a delay to your next attack. The
heavier the object, the longer the delay before you can next cast a spell, use
a skill or hit with your weapon.

Examples:

  > get sword corpse
  > get all corpse
  > get all all.bag
  > get all.bread all.bag

See Also: DROP PUT
#
GIVE

Usage: give <object> <victim>
       give <number> coins <victim>

If you feel benevolent, you may give some stuff to someone in need.

  > give all ras
  > give bread doctor
  > give all.bronze mirlen
  > give 40000 coins nia
#
GOLD

Usage: gold

Displays how much gold you have.
Gold is the primary currency in Dark Pawns and can be used to buy
services, goods, and bribes to city officials and religious institutions.

See Also: BALANCE DEPOSIT WITHDRAW
#
HOLD

Usage: hold <object>

For getting a good grip on something; a torch, for example.

Example:

  > hold torch

See Also: EQUIPMENT REMOVE WEAR WIELD
#
GROINRIP

Usage: groinrip <victim>

A popular street-fighting move, this dirty little trick leaves 'em puking 
in the aisles. The victim can be male only, of course.
#
GROUP

Usage: group [player]
       group all

GROUP with no arguments shows the status of your group.  GROUP <player>
adds or removes <player> from your group.  GROUP ALL adds everyone who is
following you to your group.

The percentage figure displayed before a group member's name is the
percentage of experience they will receive upon a mob's death. If the
mob normally gives 3000 experience, a 50% figure would give the member
1500 experience as an example. Note that the group members must be following
the leader, be grouped and be in the same room as the leader in order to
receive experience from battle.

To make a group, a "leader" must be selected.  All members of the group
must then "follow" the leader using the follow command.  The leader should
NOT follow anyone at all!  The leader can now toggle group membership for
each player in the group, by using "group <player_name>".  The leader
should remember to include himself in the group.

Example:

  Quifael and Redferne wishes to group with Dragon.

  Quifael : "follow dragon"
  Redferne: "follow dragon"
  (Dragon should be following no one but himself)
  Dragon  : "group dragon"
  Dragon  : "group redferne"
  Dragon  : "group quifael"

Later when Dragon gets upset at Quifael (because he is sleeping all the time)
he types : "Group Quifael" to kick Quifael out of the group.

See Also: EXPERIENCE UNGROUP XP
#
GSAY GTELL

Usage: gsay <message>
       gtell <message>

Tell something to all the members of your group, even if they're not in the
room.

See Also: GROUP TELL SAY
#
GUARD

Usage: guard <player|mobile>

You can specify a player or mobile to guard against harm. Should that
individual be attacked in your presence, you will automatically jump
to their aid.

Examples:
  > guard mercenary  
  You elect to be the mercenary's guardian.

  > guard
  You are guarding a mercenary.

  > guard self
  You are no longer a mercenary's guardian.

#
HEADBUTT

Usage: headbutt <victim>

Put the hurtin' on 'em! (But wear protection!)
A successful headbutt can leave the victim reeling, as well as doing
a nice amount of damage.
#
HELP ?

Usage: help [command]
       ? [command]

Help searches for a partial match of the entered word, including any
spaces that may follow the word.  Help alone will give a list of the
most common commands in the game.

Examples:

  > help magic mis
    will find the help text for the magic missile spell.

  > help mag
    will match 'magic user' or 'magic missile' depending on first
    occurrence in the help file.

  > ? help
    will give you this help file

See Also: COMMANDS SOCIALS
#
HIDE

You can attempt to conceal yourself in a room. If hidden, you can only be
seen by those with the "sense life" spell, although your identity will
remain hidden.

If you perform any action while hidden, there is a good chance that you
will be discovered, but it is possible to do things and remain hidden.

See Also: SNEAK "SENSE LIFE"
#
HOUSE

The HOUSE command is used to add or remove guests from your house's guest
list.  You must be standing in your house to use this command.  Only the
primary owner of a house (not guests) may change the guest list using the
HOUSE command.

Usage: house [<player name>]

Typing 'house' with no arguments gives a list of the people currently on
your house's guest list.  Typing 'house' with the name of a player will add
that player to your guest list if the player is not on the list, or will
remove the player from the guest list if the player is already on the list.
The player specified must be in the player database for the MUD, although
he or she does not necessarily have to be logged on at the time.

Guests of your house will be able to enter your house until you remove them
from the guest list.

See Also: CASTLES QUEST
#
INACTIVE

Usage: inactive

This command toggles your "inactive" status. While inactive, you don't get
hungry or thirsty, but you don't heal or regenerate movement or mana, either.

#
INFO NEWS POLICY VERSION FUTURE

These commands show you important information about Dark Pawns.  It is a good
idea to read them every once in a while.

   info     - useful information about the game for beginners
   faq      - even more of the same useful information
   news     - latest changes to the code and areas
   policy   - policies on topics like player killing, multis, etc.
   credits  - the DikuMUD credits
   version  - displays the current Dark Pawns release number
   future   - what new things are coming down the line

#
INFOBAR 

Usage: infobar
       infobar <on | off>

This will allow a status bar to develop on your screen.  It assumes a
24 lines by default screen.  Helpful information will be there instead
of in your prompt.  It can be resized with the "lines" command.

See Also: LINES
#
INVENTORY

Usage: inventory

Lists all the gear that you are carrying.  If you want to see what you are
wearing instead, type EQUIPMENT.

See Also: EQUIPMENT HOLD REMOVE WEAR
#
JUNK

Usage: junk <object>
       junk <number> coins

Use JUNK instead of DROP if you want to keep the world a little cleaner.  If
you JUNK something, it will disappear and you'll get a few coins or experience
points, just as if you had dropped it in the dump. Note: Items accidently
junked will not be reimbursed to you...be careful before you act!

Only those items in your inventory can be junked - to junk an item you are
wearing, it must first be removed. As a warning, if you are wearing a robe
(referred to as "robe") and have a second robe in your inventory (referred
to as "2.robe"), then attempting to "junk robe" will in fact remove the one
from your inventory. Junking a container will also junk all of its contents,
so be warned!

Examples:

  > junk cup
  > junk all.bronze
  > junk 500 coins

See Also: DONATE DROP
#
KABUKI
Usage	:	kabuki	

Named after the ancient Oriental play-acting, this skill hides the user, if
successful. You can only been sensed by the "sense life" spell, or seen by
a thorough search (The seeker types "look at <your name here>", for example.)
If you perform any actions while using kabuki, you will be discovered.  However,
there is a small chance that you will be able to perform certain actions and 
still remain hidden.
#
KICK

Usage: kick <victim>

The success of a kick depends upon how well you are learned.  The higher
level you reach the harder you kick. 

See Also: BASH RESCUE
#
KILL

Usage: kill <victim>

A good way to start a fight.  Not a good idea to hit other players.

See Also: FLEE WIMPY PK POLICY
#
KUJI-KIRI RIN KYO TOH SHA KAI JIN RETSU ZAI ZHEN

Kuji-Kiri ("nine ways cutting") is a form of mystical meditation involving
finger interlacing. The ninja is taught nine different ways to interlace
his fingers, each with its own symbolic significance. By meditating on this
gesture, the ninja can grant himself certain powers of a temporary (about 5
game hours) nature.

Power - Meaning                            - Affect
-----   -------                              ------
Rin   - "protection"                       - armors the ninja
Kyo   - "direction of energy"              - performance in battle increases
Toh   - "force and vulnerability"          - more power, less defense
Sha   - "healing"                          - hit points increase
Kai   - "the strength within"              - less power, more defense
Zhen  - "endurance"                        - vitality increases
Retsu - "mastery of time and space"        - ninja teleports 
Zai   - "the mask of illusion"             - ninja becomes invisible
Jin   - "regeneration"                     - increased healing

Usage:  rin
	  kyo
	  toh
	  etc....
#
LEARN

Usage: learn <teacher> [skill]

In order to improve your character's abilities, you must 'learn' skills
from a qualified teacher. Typing 'learn' with the teacher's name will
list those skills that can be taught, or specifying a skill will improve
your knowledge in that area...provided you have enough gold to pay for
the lesson and enough experience to progress to the next skill level.
Typing 'learn' by itself will display the skills and spells that you
currently know, your skill/spell group level and proficiency, and the
amount of mana it will cost to cast your spells.

Examples:

   > learn			- list the skills and spells that you know
   > learn muntara		- list the groups that muntara can teach
   > learn muntara protection	- increase your knowledge of protection

&gWhat does it mean:&n
&c* I am unfamiliar with that group.&n
  You have asked to learn a spell or skill group that the teacher doesn't
  know.

&c* You are not ready to advance your knowledge in this area. &n
  You don't have sufficient group points to learn this group.

&c* You lack the experience required to learn this group.&n
  Your unassigned experience is too low to learn this group.

If you have made a mistake, or no longer wish to retain a skill or spell
group, you can 'remove' that group in the presence of a teacher and have
the group points returned to you.

Usage: remove <skill/spell group>

Example:

   If you had level 2 of the Astral spell group, and decided you didn't want
   it anymore, you could type 'remove astral' in front of a teacher and you
   would regain 2 group points to be used on something else.

See Also: SKILLS TEACHER "GROUP POINTS" REMOVE
#
LEAVE

Usage: leave

If you feel claustrophobic, typing 'leave' will make you use the nearest
obvious exit to the outside.

See Also: ENTER
#
LINES

Usage: lines
       lines <number>

Allows you to set the number of lines you have to your screen.  It can
range anywhere from 7 to 50 inclusive.  Without an argument, this
command will tell you what your current screen is set at.  This number
is only used in the infobar and OLC for immorts.

See Also: INFOBAR
#
LIST

Usage: list [item type]

If you'd like to see what items a shop has for sale, take a look at the
list.  The list contains all of the items currently for sale and in
what quantity.  The price for each item is also listed.  If you are
interested in a particular type of item, you can specify which items to
list.

Weapons displayed as "lack requirement" indicate that you will be unable
to wield the weapon given your current skill.

Examples:
 
  > list             (list all items for sale)
  > list sword       (list all swords for sale)
 
See Also: BUY SELL SHOPS VALUE REQUIREMENT
#
LOOK

Usage: look
       look [in | at] [the] <item>
       look <direction>

For studying your surroundings.

Examples:

  > look                                      
  > look AT the angel
  > look IN the bag
  > look south (May give some information as to what is south)

Note that if you LOOK AT CORPSE you will not see its inventory.
To see what's inside a container (i.e. a corpse) use LOOK IN <object>.

Looking in directions will show you either a description of the door
in that direction (if any), a generalized one line description of what
lies in that direction, or the actual room itself.  Players may turn off 
full room listings while using look [direction] by playing in BRIEF mode.

See Also: GET READ BRIEF
#
CHECK MAIL RECEIVE MUDMAIL

Usage: check
       mail <person>
       receive
       
The commands used by the Dark Pawns Mail System (DPMS) are MAIL, CHECK, and
RECEIVE.  These commands can only be used while in an Official DPMS Post
Office.  You must be at least second level in order to use the DPMS.

Examples:

  To check and see if you have any mail waiting:
  > check

  To write mail to Niandra:
  > mail Niandra

  To ask the Postmaster to give you your mail, if you have any waiting:
  > receive

Stamps cost 25 coins.

#
MINDLINK "MIND LINK"

By establishing a mental link with your victim, you are able to drain them
of life to increase your mana. Should it be unsuccessful, you can drain
a significant amount of health from your victim but receive no benefit from
the link.
#
MIX

Usage: mix <container>

Provided you have studied alchemy, this command will allow you to mix
ingredients to form your own magickal potions and other various things.
There are a few requirements for the mixing to be successful:

  * You must have a container to mix reagents in (a mortar is the
    best for the job)

  * You need an empty vial in which to store your completed product

  * Your container must have the necessary ingredients within it

See Also: ALCHEMY POTION INGREDIENTS

#
MOTD

Usage: motd

Displays the message of the day.  Contains important information
regarding the status of the MUD.  You should be sure to read it
when you login.  If you miss it at login, just use this command!

See Also: INFO NEWS
#
MXP MSP MCCP

Usage: toggle mxp

The mud sound protocol (MSP), mud extension protocol (MXP) and mud client
compression protocol (MCCP) add a new dimension to the game. Provided your
mud client is capable of MSP/MXP, you will be able to experience sound and
graphical enchancements to your game play. MCCP, MXP and MSP are automatically
enabled, but only MXP can be toggled to disabled. MCCP is a behind-the-
scenes tool and should not affect any aspect of your game play.

If you wish to disable either MXP or MSP manually, refer to your mud client
documentation and do so through the mud client.

See Also: TOGGLE
#
NECKBREAK

Usage: neckbreak <victim>

The trained master of ninjitsu can execute a one-time attempt to break his
victims neck quickly.  Success deals nearly lethal damage to the victim, 
failures are usually quite messy.

#
NEWBIE
 
Newbie is a term used to describe people who are new to MUDding, and sometimes
just one particular MUD. As a newbie you start out with a few choice pieces
of equipment and enough food to last until you gather enough money to buy
more. The INFO and POLICY commands will tell you the rules and basics of
Dark Pawns, and the NEWS file will keep you updated on various added features.
Also, check out help FAQ, which has the answers to some of frequently asked
newbie questions.

You will start out in the Temple of your home town. You should spend some time
becoming familiar with the commands available to you, and you can stop your
hunger and thirst (while you study) using the INACTIVE command.

When you're ready, you can begin exploring the realm - don't venture too far
from the city gates as the wilderness is no place for a newbie! Find some of
the local wildlife to improve your combat skills, as you will need the
EXPERIENCE in order to progress in level. Note that killing within any city
limits is frowned upon by the town guards and you will most likely be
jailed for the offence.

Renting here is free, but only in certain areas, the main one being the Temple
and Altar in the city of Kir Drax'in.

See Also: FAQ NEWS POLICY MULTI MAP EXPERIENCE
#
NOREPEAT

Usage: toggle repeat

This command determines whether or not you see your communication echoed
back to you (i.e., from commands such as SAY, SHOUT, HOLLER, GOSSIP, etc.)
Useful if you have a slow connection or if it just annoys you.

See Also: TOGGLE
#
NORTH SOUTH EAST WEST UP DOWN

Usage: north
       south
       east
       west
       up
       down

To travel in a given direction. To see directions available for travel, 
use EXITS or better yet AUTO EXIT.

See Also: EXIT AUTO
#
NOSHOUT

Usage: toggle shout

Determines whether or not you hear the shouts of others.  (deaf) will appear
after your name in the WHO list.

See Also: FLAGS HOLLER SHOUT TOGGLE WHO
#
NOTELL

Usage: toggle tell

Use this if you wish to prevent other players from using "tell" to
communicate with you.  (notell) will appear after your name in the WHO
list if you have notell on.

See Also: FLAGS TELL TOGGLE WHO
#
RENT

There is no RENT on Dark Pawns.  Your items are automatically saved
when you QUIT at no cost.

See Also: QUIT
#
OPEN CLOSE LOCK UNLOCK

Usage: open | close | lock | unlock <door> [direction]

To open, close, lock, and unlock doors, of course.

Examples:

  > open portal
  > lock door
  > unlock door south
  > close gate

See Also: ENTER LEAVE
#
ORDER

Usage: order <character> <command>
       order followers <command>

Used for ordering pets and charmed people to do your evil bidding.  You
can order everyone under your command with "order followers".

Examples:

  > order puppy eat bread
  > order cityguard sleep
  > order followers kill Link

See Also: CHARM
#
PALM

Usage	:	palm <item in room>

Used for getting an item without getting noticed. A successful palm of an
item lets you acquire it (to your inventory) with no one noticing. A 
failed palm is just like a normal "get <object>". 

Only items in the room can be palmed, not objects in containers. The 
smaller the object, the easier it is to palm.

See Also: STEAL
#
PARRY

Usage: parry

Used to strike a defensive stance and parry (counter) the attacks of your
opponent. Most effective on opponents with multiple attacks. A successful
parry will counter one of your opponents attacks.

Parry is sometimes automatic once you have learned the skill.  It occurs 
reflexively in combat, with greater skill providing more frequent parries.
#
PEEK

Usage: peek <victim>

When being caught staring could be bad for your health, peek lets you size
up your victim without being noticed. A failed peek is just like a normal
"look <victim>"; however it's hard to tell if you're noticed. (Unless of 
course, they start pounding on you.) Note that you will only be able to
see what other players are carrying, not mobs.
#
"PICK LOCKS" LOCKS LOCKPICKS PICKS

Usage: pick <lock name> [direction]

For picking locks.  Not all locks can be picked. Those that can require a
set of held lockpicks. Lockpicks can be found in most major cities and are
usually very cheap. (Unfortunately, the quality is usually the same as the
price.) As your experience picking locks grows, the chance of mangling your
lockpicks lessens.

Examples:

  > pick door south
  > pick safe

See Also: OPEN CLOSE LOCK UNLOCK
#
POINT

Usage:  point
	point <victim>
	point <object>
	point <direction>

Used for... pointing things out.
Remember what your mother said however... its not nice to point.
#
POUR

Usage: pour <from container> <to container>
       pour <from container> out

If you want to pour some liquid from one container to another.  Pouring
out simply empties the contents of the container onto the ground.

Examples:

  > pour canteen cup
  > pour cup out

See Also: FILL, DRINK
#
PRACTISE PRACTICE

This command has been replaced by the LEARN command.

See Also: LEARN
#
PUT

Usage: put <item> <container>
       put all.<item> <container>
       put all <container>

For putting items into containers.

Examples:

  > put bread bag
  > put all.bread bag
  > put all chest

See Also: GET
#
SCOUT

Usage: scout <direction>

This can be useful in finding difficult to track persons, as well as
assessing the size of an enemy force and avoiding certain natural
pitfalls.
#
SEARCH SECRET DOORS DOOR DETECT

Usage: search    

Using this command, an adventurer calls upon his skills in detection,
surveying every inch of the room for a secret door or hidden entrance.
#
SHARPEN

Usage: sharpen <bladed weapon>

This skill works only on bladed weapons of a certain quality. 
Magickal blades can not be sharpened. Sharpened blades do more damage.
#
SLEEPER

Usage    : sleeper <victim>
Duration : Varies with level

The legendary sleeper hold. Just grab your opponent by the neck and soon
its sleepy time for them. Zzzzz.

Note: Sleeper works best on humanoid-types and some people may be too big
or too strong to knock unconscious using this method. Also, you must be 
bare-handed to sleeper someone.
#
SPIKE STAKE

Usage: spike <werewolf name>
       stake <vampire name>

You must be holding the correct spike or stake for your form of beastly
target, and it must be done while the target is in beastly form.
A failed save throw by the beast results in immediate, painful
death and loss of beastliness. Do not pass go, do not collect $200.00.

See Also: WEREWOLF VAMPIRE
#
SQUELCH

Usage: squelch <character>

If someone is annoying you, the easiest way to ignore them is with squelch!
By adding someone to your squelch list, you will not see the majority of
the things they do or say. You are allowed a maximum of 5 people in your
squelch list.
#
SUBDUE

Usage: subdue <victim>

When you don't want to kill them (right away), subdue them. This command,
When executed successfully, leaves the victim stunned and unable to move 
until the next tick of the game clock. A successful subdue maneuver leaves
the victim unknowing who subdued them.
#
QSAY

Usage: qsay <message>

To tell something to everyone on the current Quest.

See Also: QUEST
#
QUEST

Usage: toggle quest

This simple toggle command merely informs the Powers that Be that you
wish to participate in the currently running Quest.  If an immortal
is running a Quest and needs to know who wishes to participate, he/she
will ask players to turn on their Quest flags using this QUEST command
if they are interested in the Quest.  It also allows you to listen in on
the quest channel and receive information specific to the quest.

See Also: QSAY
#
QUI SHUTDOW

Just to prevent accidental quittings and/or shutdowns.
This command doesn't DO anything, it simply is.

See Also: QUIT
#
QUIT

When you get tired of playing, you can leave the game by typing 'quit'.
Your equipment is saved automatically once your character has left the game.

You will return to the room you quit from, when you decide to return to
the game. Keep in mind, although you may quit when nobody or nothing is
nearby, when you return, you could find yourself surrounded by an angry
hoard of monsters.

See Also: HOMETOWN RECALL "WORD OF RECALL"
#
RECHARGE RECHARGER

Find the recharger and he will recharge your staves and wands, 
for a price.  Recharging decreases the max charges for the object.
The recharger himself has more info on the subject.

#
REFUGE

Usage : refuge

Allows those players adequately trained to create a natural place of safety
for themselves and the members of their group (if there are any). This skill
can only be used in forest or mountainous areas where there is enough
material to make a refuge. It has the same restrictions upon it as per the HIDE
skill.

See Also: HIDE
#
RSAY

Usage: rsay <sentence>

Rsay (race-say) lets you speak in your own native tongue. Those 
not of your race see a gibberish-type message. Careful.. this message
IS decipherable.

See Also: RACE
#
READ

Usage: read <object>
       read <board message number>

When you want to read something.

READ is also used to read messages on bulletin boards; type HELP BOARDS
for more information.

Example:

  > read note

See Also: BOARDS
#
RECALL

Usage: recall

This command will recall you to the last place you bound your spirit.
Certain rooms will prevent you from using this command and you cannot use
it while engaged in battle.

See Also: "WORD OF RECALL" QUIT HOMETOWN
#
RECITE SCROLL SCROLLS
 
Usage: recite <scroll> [Target]
 
Is used to "read" a magical scroll.  Target can be an object, character or
nothing (which defaults to yourself). When read, scrolls will dissolve. Some 
scrolls may contain more than one spell.

IMPORTANT NOTE: Recall scrolls *cannot* be used during combat. You *must* be
out of battle to use a recall scroll.
 
See Also: SPELLS MAGICK
#
REMOVE

Usage: remove <item>
       remove all
       remove all.<keyword>
       remove <skill/spell group>

If you tire of wearing some armor or wielding a weapon, remove it.

Examples:

  > remove boots
  > remove sword
  > remove all
  > remove all.bronze

Alternatively, you can remove a known skill or spell group (in the presence
of a teacher) and have the group points returned to you. However, you will
not regain the unassigned experience or the gold that you had previously
spent.

See Also: HOLD WEAR WIELD LEARN
#
REPLY .

Usage: reply <message>
       . <message>

This command will send a reply to the last person to send you a message
using TELL.  It works just as if you had typed 'tell <player> <message>'
but makes it a bit easier.  It can also be very useful in case someone
invisible sends you a message.

Example:

Ras tells you, 'Hi!'
> reply hey
You tell Ras, 'hey'
>
Someone tells you, 'I am your secret admirer.'
> . Who are you?
You tell someone, 'Who are you?'

See Also: TELL NOTELL
#
REPORT

Usage: report

This command sends a report of your current health, as well as other
general statistics, to everyone in the room that you are currently in.

If used in a player-owned store, the shop keeper will indicate how much
gold the store carries.

See Also: OWNER
#
RESCUE

Usage: rescue <victim>

This command is useful if you want to try and make an attacker hit you
instead of your poor friend who is being pummeled.  You can only 'turn'
one monster for each rescue attempt.  This is very useful when playing
in groups, of course.

Example:

> rescue Yankee
#
RETRIEVE

Usage: retrieve

You can retrieve your corpse for a price at any skilled Mortician in the
realms.  These Morticians are known to be few and far between however.
Also, certain practitioners of the Black Arts are known to be able to
retrieve corpses, but their motives are probably less than respectable.

See Also: DEATH CORPSE
# 
RETREAT

Usage: retreat

Retreat is an advanced version of the FLEE command and performs the same
function, however it can only be used in battle. It also suffers no lag
and can be used at any stage of a fight. If your WIMPY is triggered during
battle and you are familiar with the skill, you may be able to retreat
instead of fleeing.

See Also: FLEE WIMPY
#
REVIEW

Usage: review <gossip | auction>

Lets you review the last 25 gossip or auction messages.

See Also: GOSSIP
#
MOUNT MOUNTS

Usage: mount <mount name>

Examples: 

   > mount horse
   > mount cammel

Used to mount your favorite mode of transport. Most mounts are not welcome within
city limits (health regulations and all...) so you will need to STABLE your mount
if you wish to retain it.

See Also: DISMOUNT STABLE
#
SAVE

Usage: save

This command is used to save your aliases only, which is done automatically
every minute. It does not save information about your character, or any of
your equipment - this function is also performed automatically.

See Also: ALIAS QUIT
#
SAY TALK TELL WHISPER SHOUT HOLLER '

Usage: say | shout | holler <string>
       tell | whisper <player> <string>

If you consider communicating with other beings, you might be understood
better if you start your sentences with either say, tell, whisper or shout.

Examples:

  > say Hey, does anyone know how to get to Oz?
  > tell catje hi, how are you?

You can use ' as a shorthand for say, as in:

  > ' hello there.

Shout broadcasts your message to everyone is your geographic zone.  Holler
broadcasts to everyone in the game but costs 20 movement points.  You must
be level 2 before you can use shout or holler.

See Also: AUCTION GOSSIP GSAY NOREPEAT QSAY REPLY
#
SCORE

Usage: score

Provides useful information on your status such as age, hit points,
mana, movement points, armor class, alignment, experience points, gold
on hand, how long you've been playing, and your level.

See Also: AC EXPERIENCE SPELLS ABILITIES "GROUP POINTS" "ABILITY POINTS"
          VITAE
#
SCRIBE

Usage: scribe <object> '<spell name>'

Allows you to create your own scrolls, used in conjunction with SOUL TRAP.
The object must be something that can be written on, and the most commonly
available item would be a piece of parchment (available in all cities). The
spell name must be enclosed by "'"s, and must be a spell that you are
familiar with. It must also be a spell that is castable only upon
yourself (such as heal, or word of recall).

You must be in possession of, and holding, a soul gem in order to use this
skill. The soul gem must also contain a soul, as obtained using the SOUL
TRAP spell.

Examples:

   > scribe parchment 'detect align'
   > scribe note 'meteor swarm'

See Also: "SOUL TRAP"
#
SCROUNGE

Usage: scrounge

Those skilled in the art can scrounge up a meal anywhere, just by feeding
off of the land.
#
SELL

Usage: sell [#] <item>
       sell <#>.<item>

If you'd like to sell an item to a shopkeeper, trying selling it to them.
Most shops specialize in what they will buy, so you may have to look around
to find a buyer for your items.
 
Examples:
 
  > sell sword       (sell the first sword in your inventory)
  > sell 3 sword     (sell the first three swords in your inventory)
  > sell all.scroll  (sell all of the scrolls in your inventory)
 
See Also: BUY LIST SHOPS VALUE
#
"SERPENT KICK"

Usage: serpent <victim>

This punishing, lethal kick is part of the Golden Serpent Kung Fu style, and
knowledge of it is forbidden outside the Liu'she Ch'uan tong. Learning it
earns a sentence of death from any tong member. Beware.
#
SHADOW

Usage: shadow <victim>

Use this command to unobtrusively follow your victim. When used in conjunction
with the sneak and hide skills, a successful shadower can be virtually 
undetectable.

See Also: FOLLOW
#
SKIN

Usage: skin <corpse>

Use this command to remove the hide of an animal - of course, it has to be
dead in order for you to do it!  You must be wielding an appropriate weapon in
order to remove the hide.
#
SLEEP

SLEEP is both a command and the name of a spell.

The SLEEP command puts you to sleep, allowing you to regain your health more
quickly.  You will be largely unaware of your surroundings while asleep.
You can awaken yourself with the WAKE command. You will need sleep from time
to time, as per most beings, in order to remain at your peak!

The SLEEP spell forces the victim into a magical sleep such that they 
cannot be awakened until the spell wears off.

Usage    : cast 'sleep' <victim>
Duration : Varies with the caster's level
Group    : Utility
Mana     : 100 - 150

If failing saving throw versus spell, the person will fall asleep.
A person who is affected by sleep can only be awakened if attacked.

See Also: WAKE
#
SLUG

Usage: slug <victim>

This is a devastating blow, used by the bare-handed individual to rattle
a little sense into the victim.
#
SMACKHEADS

Usage: smackheads <victim1> <victim2>

Ex:     smackheads warg janitor
        smackheads cityguard 2.cityguard

Grab some hair and bash their brains! Only thing more satisfying than 
smacking two heads together is... well, there's not much more satisfying
in battle, at least.

See Also: COMBAT
#
SNEAK

Usage: sneak

Used for sneaking (moving in and out of rooms without anyone taking notice).
When you type sneak, there is no way to know if you're actually sneaking.
If you successfully sneak, then you'll continue to sneak for a little while.

See Also: HIDE STEALTH
#
SPLIT

Usage: split <amount to split>

Split is used to split money among people in your group who are in the same
room as you.  If you are in a group with 4 other people, all of whom are in
the same room with you, and you type SPLIT 100, you will give each of the
other 4 group members 20 coins each.  (100 coins is split 5 ways; you keep
your share and give everyone else their share).

See Also: FOLLOW GROUP GOLD
#
STABLE

Usage: stable

Stable is used to stable your mount for a nominal daily fee and is a much
cheaper option than buying a fresh mount. Of course, you can only stable
your mount in an appropriate location and only with qualified people.

See Also: MOUNT DISMOUNT
#
STEAL

Usage: steal <item> <victim>

Use steal to steal gold or items from people.  The chance of not getting
caught depends on how high your skill level is, and if the person is
asleep.

Stealing from players is probably not a good idea at all.

Examples:

  > steal gold drunk
  > steal sword mercenary
    (If it's wielded, only possible if he is sleeping)

See Also: FLAGS PSTEAL
#
"STRIKE OF REVENGE"

Usage	: strike <victim>

Allows the trained martial artist to deal a stunning, sometimes lethal 
Strike to the victim's throat.

Developed by the Mist Viper school of Ninjitsu, "Saito Yuriko's Strike of
Revenge" is a brutal, devastating blow.

See Also: COMBAT
#
TAG IT

Usage: tag <player>

They're IT!
Used to start a game of tag or tag another player after you have been tagged IT.
#
"TIGER PUNCH" TIGER

Usage: tiger <victim>

This devastating uppercut can do serious damage to the victim if they are unable
to block it.  The tiger punch is a more aggressive style of ninja combat, used 
when the ninja cannot avoid direct confrontation.

#
THINK

Usage: think <message>

Lets others see what you're thinking!

See Also: SOCIALS
#
TIME

Usage: time

Gives you the current game time.  Your initial reaction to the output of
this command may be one of surprise, but you'll get used to it.  You'll
have to, at any rate, since certain things in the game depend on this
particular notion of time; the opening hours of the shops, for example.

Also listed is the phase of the moon; this is important to VAMPIREs and
WEREWOLVES, as the fullness of the moon decides the bonuses they get (mana
and hit points, respectively.) During the nights of a full moon, they are 
forced to TRANSFORM. Moon phase also affects MOONGATES.

See Also: WEREWOLF VAMPIRE TRANSFORM MOONGATE GATE
#
TITLE

Usage: title <new title>

Sets the title people see on the WHO list and when you're in the room with
them.  You can't use parentheses (the "(" and ")" characters) because those
are reserved for flags.

Do not abuse this command; if you do, it will be taken from you.

See Also: FLAGS WHO
#
TOGGLE

Usage: toggle

TOGGLE shows you the current values of various toggles available on the MUD.
All of these toggles remain the same until you change them; i.e. they are
saved when you quit or rent.

Not all of the displayed values can be altered with the toggle command,
but generally those with YES/NO or ON/OFF values can be controlled via
this command.

See Also: AUTO BRIEF COMPACT DISPLAY NOSHOUT NOTELL QUEST MXP
          NOREPEAT WIMP
#
TRACK

Usage: track <victim>

Used for finding the first step on the shortest route to another person. A 
Failed attempt results in the wrong direction.  Some people are more 
difficult to track than others. Tracking also doesn't work very well when
it is raining outside, or if there is a body of water separating you from
your target.

Example:

  > track warg
  You sense a trail south from here!

See Also: EVASION
#
TRANSFORM

Usage: transform

This command allows lycanthropes and vampires to change form from common
man into nightbreed. Beast-shape can only be assumed during the night
hours, and only be shed during the day -- once you transform, there's no 
going back until the next dusk/dawn.

See Also: VAMPIRE LYCANTHROPE TIME STAKE SPIKE
#
TRIP

Usage: trip <victim>

Causes the victim to fall, subsequently delaying their ability to fight
back.

See Also: COMBAT
#
TURN

With this power, you can cause undead forces in the same room to flee from
your presence.  This power varies with level, and low level players may not
be able to turn away certain powerful (ie: demonic) undead forces. On the
upside, very powerful spell casters are able to completely destroy lesser
undead.

Please note that this is a SKILL, not a SPELL, although it does consume
MANA. The amount of mana consumed is proportional to your level.

See Also: COMBAT
#
UNGROUP

Usage: ungroup [group member]

UNGROUP can be used by group leaders to disband the entire group, or
to kick a specific group member out of the group (and stop him/her from
following the leader).

Examples:

  > ungroup
  > ungroup homer

See Also: GROUP
#
USE

There are many objects within the game that can be used and it will be up
to you to discover most of them. Depending on the function of these items,
they may require you to HOLD them, or they may simply be in your inventory.

See Also: WAND STAFF RECITE
#
VALUE

Usage: value <item>

Before selling an item to a shop, you can ask the shopkeeper how much
he or she is willing to pay for it.
 
Example:
 
  > value bread
 
See Also: BUY LIST SELL SHOPS
#
VISIBLE

Usage: visible

Use this command to break your spell of invisibility before it expires, or
to stop sneaking.

See Also: INVISIBILITY SNEAK STEALTH
#
WAKE SLEEPING REST SIT STAND

Commands for changing your position.  If you feel weary, it's probably 
a good idea to sit and rest for a while, or maybe even take a nap.

The SLEEP command puts you to sleep, allowing you to regain your health 
more quickly.  You will be largely unaware of your surroundings while 
asleep. You can awaken yourself (and others) with the WAKE command.

Also, certain rooms such as holy rooms and places of ancient power allow
you to heal and regenerate faster.

#
WEAR

Usage: wear <item> [location]

Use this if you want to wear some clothes, armor or the like.

Also, to wear everything in your inventory (or at least try to, as wearing 
things like loaves of bread is not a good way to win friends and influence
people) you can type "wear all".

Optionally, you can specify what part of your body to wear the equipment 
on.

Examples:

  > wear boots
  > wear all.bronze
  > wear all
  > wear ring finger

 If you have more than one pair in your inventory
  > wear 2.boots 

See Also: EQUIPMENT REMOVE
#
WEATHER

Usage: weather

If you're uncertain whether the sun is shining or the rain is 
pouring down. You'll have to be outside in order to tell however.

See Also: "CONTROL WEATHER"
#
WHO

Usage: who [minlev[-maxlev]] [-n sname] [-s] [-o] [-q]

Lists the people currently in the game.  Some people may be invisible.
Command-line options can be used to limit the listing.  The parameters
can be specified on the command-line in any order.

minlev, maxlev : list only people whose level is at or above minlev, and
                 optionally, at or below maxlev
-n : list only people whose names or titles contain sname
-s : list names in the short form (4 columns of names, without titles or
     flags)
-o : list only outlaws
-q : list only people who are on the Quest

Examples:

  > who 15-25 -o 
  List all outlaws between levels 15 and 25.

#
WHOAMI

Usage: whoami

Displays your character's name, if you want to be sure you are who
you think you are.

See Also: WHO FINGER
#
WIELD

Usage: wield <weapon>

When you get tired of bashing monsters with your fists, you might consider
wielding a weapon. Some weapons may have a skill requirement, that require
(funnily enough) a certain level of proficiency in order to wield them.

Example:

  > wield sword
  > wield 3.sword    (Wield the third sword in your inventory)

See Also: EQUIPMENT REMOVE WEAR REQUIREMENT
#
WIMPY

Usage: wimpy [hp]

Use the WIMPY command to automatically flee once your health drops below
a certain level. Note that you can't flee if you are not standing.

Examples:

  > wimpy 35    will make your character automatically flee a fight
                if you have less than 35 hit points.
  > wimpy 0     will turn off wimpy mode.
  > wimpy       will show you your current wimp status.

If you have not learned the RETREAT skill, you will attempt to FLEE. Note
that the RETREAT skill is not affected by combat wait, whereas the FLEE
ability is!

See Also: COMBAT RETREAT FLEE
#
WIZLIST IMMLIST

Usage: wizlist | immlist

Lists the most powerful beings on the MUD.  These are the people
responsible for the background operation of Dark Pawns.

See Also: IMPLEMENTOR
#
WRITE

Usage: write <object>
       write <title of board note>

In order to write a note, you need a piece of blank paper (or similar), and
a pen of some sort.  You can then type something like "write on the paper with
the pen", whereupon you'll be asked to type in your note at the keyboard.

WRITE is also used to post messages to bulletin boards.  Type HELP BOARDS
for more information.

See Also: BOARDS MAIL
#
YANK

Usage: yank <victim>

For those slow-to-move group members, you can yank them onto their feet.

See Also: GROUP
#
$
